  "query_preview": "/FRIDAY THROUGH WEDNESDAY/...\nIssued at 229 PM CST Wed Nov 25 2026\n\n(Friday - Saturday)\n\nA moderating trend is expected Friday into Saturday with \ntemperatures getting back close to normal. Dry weather is also\nforecast.\n\n\n(Saturday Night - Sunday)\n\nEnsemble guidance shows another deepening mid/upper level trough \nmoving across the south-central Plains into the Mississippi Valley \nSaturday night into Sunday. This system is further to the north with \nless cold air to work with than its predecessor, so only a cold rain \nis expected at this time. Widespread light rain though is likely,\nwith probabilities from the LREF for at least a tenth of an \ninch of rain greater than 60% areawide. While not looking like a\nsignificant precipitation producer, a rain event a few days \nafter a very widespread heavy precipitation event is certainly \ngood in terms of drought improvement. \n\n\n(Sunday Night - Next Wednesday)\n\nBehind the late weekend system, a return to slightly below normal \ntemperatures is expected with highs in the 40s/50s and lows in the \n20s/30s. Dry weather is also expected, though a weaker midlevel wave \nmay have the potential to bring some light rain to parts of the area \nas soon as Tuesday.",
